 need for me use 5 chargers one charger is good\",\"source\":\"crawler\",\"sort_order\":1,\"create_time\":1792206781},{\"comment_id\":334109942,\"user_name\":\"KRISHNA\",\"rating\":5,\"content\":\"Very fast laptop charging with PD 3.1\\nFour ports—great for charging several devices together\\nBuilt-in display shows charging information and temperature\\nGood for laptops such as MacBook Pro/Air and other USB-C laptops\",\"source\":\"crawler\",\"sort_order\":2,\"create_time\":1792163736},{\"comment_id\":334109940,\"user_name\":\"DONNAW\",\"rating\":5,\"content\":\"Anker is my go to brand for charging, and this one lives up to everything I expect from them. I use it every day at my desk to keep my MacBook Pro, my phone, and the rest of my devices charged from one spot.\\n\\nThe biggest surprise for me was how much it handles at once. It has 4 ports, 3 USB C and 1 USB A, so I can plug in my laptop, my phone, and a couple of other things all at the same time. One charger took the place of a whole pile of bricks and cords.\\n\\nIt is fast, too. It can put out up to 140 watts to a single device, which is enough to charge my 16 inch MacBook Pro at full speed. When I have several things plugged in, it shares the power out on its own, so I never have to think about it.\\n\\nI also like knowing it has Anker's safety system built in, since it stays plugged in all day. And it works on 100 to 240 volts, so it can travel anywhere with me.\\n\\nIt is small for how much it does and keeps my desk so much neater. I would recommend it to anyone with more than one device to charge.\",\"source\":\"crawler\",\"sort_order\":3,\"create_time\":1791672588},{\"comment_id\":334109947,\"user_name\":\"jules\",\"rating\":5,\"content\":\"140W adapter is a great wattage for multiple products to be charged at once, this adapter also has the built in screen to check on temperature and wattage output.\\n\\nGreat charger for the price. !\",\"source\":\"crawler\",\"sort_order\":4,\"create_time\":17915929